<title>CANADA: Canada to auction C$3 billion bonds due 1999.</title>
<headline>Canada to auction C$3 billion bonds due 1999.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Government of Canada said it plans to auction on December 4, C$3.0 billion of bonds with an unspecified coupon, maturing on March 15, 1999.</p>
<p>The Bank of Canada said it will buy at least C$300 million of the new bonds.  </p>
<p>The bonds, which will be dated and delivered on December 16, pay interest on March 15 and September 15, the government said.</p>
<p>Proceeds of the issue will be used for the general purposes of the Government of Canada.</p>
<p>There are no Government of Canada marketable bonds maturing on December 16.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
